CQ_lang free-pairing analysis — pinned vendored ANALYSIS mirror
===============================================================

WHY THIS DIRECTORY EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS NOT `third_party/cq_lang/`.

`bd 06t` and PRD-v1.md §15 D15 §2 both instruct the implementer to PORT
upstream's free-pairing reduction — `reduces_to_identity`, `unchanged_over`,
`pair_operands_unchanged`, `co_written_stable` — and NOT to re-derive its
parity, on the recorded ground that upstream had a live miscompile in exactly
that reduction and fixed it on 2026-08-11 with those dedicated guards.

Measured 2026-08-27, before any of that work started: NONE of those four
strings appeared anywhere under `third_party/`. They live in CQ_lang, which
this repository does not pin — `third_party/cq_lang/` holds `opcode_table.yaml`
and a COMMIT naming `a6a92fe`, and CQ_lang's HEAD has moved well past it. So
Rule 1's "it must be on disk at a pinned commit before any kernel is written"
was NOT satisfied for the thing the bead told the implementer to port, and
every citation in `bd 06t` (`free_pairing_check.py:150-160`, `:436-448`,
`ROADMAP.md:381-386`) pointed into an unpinned tree. Reading an unpinned file
and calling the result a port is the failure Rule 16 is about; re-deriving the
parity to avoid the question is the failure Rule 1 is about. Vendoring is the
third option and it is the one taken.

SEPARATE DIRECTORY, ON PURPOSE — THREE REASONS.

  1. NO BYTE OF ANY EXISTING `third_party/` FILE CHANGES. Rule 1 clause 1
     forbids writing to `third_party/`, COMMIT included, and its stated
     rationale is that a local edit silently voids the provenance record. A new
     directory with its own honest record voids nothing: `opcode_table.yaml`'s
     sha256 is untouched, the Bennett snapshot is untouched, and
     `git status --porcelain third_party/` reports one new untracked path and
     no modification. Verified at the moment of the copy.
  2. THE TWO ARTEFACTS PIN AT DIFFERENT REVISIONS, AND ONE COMMIT FILE CANNOT
     SAY SO WITHOUT AMBIGUITY. `third_party/cq_lang/COMMIT` pins CQ_lang HEAD
     at `a6a92fe`; this artefact is taken at a HEAD two weeks later. Merging
     them would put two "Pinned revision (HEAD)" lines in one file, which is
     precisely the shape a drift check cannot read.
  3. IT IS A DIFFERENT KIND OF ARTEFACT. `opcode_table.yaml` is a FROZEN ABI we
     satisfy. This is an ANALYSIS we port from, exactly as `third_party/bennett`
     is a set of constructions we port from. Rule 1's model for that is a
     snapshot with a manifest, not an ABI mirror.

