WHAT IS PORTED FROM IT, AND WHAT IS NOT
---------------------------------------
  PORTED: the reduction engine and its four guards —
    reduces_to_identity          :1390
    unchanged_over               :1220
    commutes                     :1362
    pair_operands_unchanged      :1447
    co_written_stable            :1549
  and the entry conditions that hand off to them.

  NOT PORTED, and the difference is not a simplification: upstream runs over
  CQ_lang's LOWERED LLVM IR (`run_slice.sh:65` feeds it `s2.ll`), where a rail
  is an SSA name and the loop algebra is still present. libcqops sees a CALL
  STREAM of opaque handles and nothing else. Every place the port is WEAKER
  than upstream must be weaker in the UNPROVEN direction — never in the
  proven-clean direction — because an over-discharge here recycles a non-|0>
  index, which `src/qubits.h` names the one unforgivable bug in this project.

